(text "TBD (not invented): which nice!nano pins receive Phob GPIO12-GPIO15 and whether the link is SPI or UART.\nUpstream gcwireless TX code (src/tx.cpp @ 576878d) has no Phob link at all: it only reads P0.17 (light\nsensor test, INPUT_PULLUP, tx.cpp lines 7 and 96) and P0.31 (power-down input, tx.cpp lines 5 and 88).\nThose two are labelled LIGHT_IN and POWEROFF_IN here; they are firmware test pins, not final wiring.\nTBD: power direction on J6 pin 1. The Phob 3.3 V rail is normally fed by +5V -> AMS1117 -> D1\n(docs/facts/phobgcc.md); feeding +3V3 from the nice!nano 3.3V pin is unverified (docs/facts/power.md).\nTBD: battery connector type (nice!nano has BATTERY+ pads; pinout page above).\nBAT+ goes to both BATTERY+ pins, as the official image shows two." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.000 40.000 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "816fd9fa-1bda-5cf2-9766-2b8da75e6260"))
(embedded_fonts no)
)
